Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Scaling backgrounds: spectra and reproducible backgrounds", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"1d9bf42c-3a83-b641-9e87-37f0b277ca73"],

Cell["\<\
Warning: Keep this notebook beside its three data JSON files. Evaluate the \
two initialisation cells, in order, to import all data and define every function. 

The notebook imports the following files:
- scaling_backgrounds.json supplies the catalogue, supersymmetry, symmetry, g \
L_AdS, eta, mass spectra and BF stability. 
- model_22_scalars.json supplies the ordered 22 scalar fields and explicit \
expressions for V, h1 and h2m. 
- backgrounds_22_scalars.json supplies their numerical values in the field \
order defined by model_22_scalars.json. \[LineSeparator]
The database contains the 78 currently known scale covariant background with \
an Index running from 1 to 78 in descending order of g L_AdS. Each background \
has an additional label Zxxxxxx using the first six digits after the decimal \
point in the numeric value of g L_AdS, without rounding.

The JSON field L_AdS stores g L_AdS from Eq. (6), evaluated at g=1. For d=3 \
and k=-2. The catalogue, background values, labels and equations all use the \
same scalar frame.

The running scalar obeys varphi_new=varphi_previous/2. In the supplied JSON, \
h1 is already multiplied by 4 and every h2m by 2; import them directly. The profile is \
varphi(r)=-eta r/(2 L_AdS), or varphi(z)=(eta/2) log(z/L_AdS), with \
z=L_AdS exp(-r/L_AdS). The reference slice varphi=0, eta, g L_AdS and \
mass spectra are unchanged. At the SO(7)/D2 point, h1=16 gives eta=1/3.

Definitions (all functions accept an index or label):
- fields lists all 22 scalars. 
- GetBackground[x] returns their numerical values in fields order. 
- ListBackgrounds[] displays Index, Label, g LAdS, eta, Continuous symmetry \
group, Discrete symmetry group, SUSY and BF stable for all backgrounds. \
Optional arguments \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]SUSY\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]BF_stable\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] restrict to the \
relevant subset of backgrounds.
- indexForLabel[\"Z666666\"] returns the index for that \
label.\[LineSeparator]- label[i] returns the label for that index.
- AdSLength[i], etaValue[i], supersymmetry[i] and globalSymmetry[i] read the \
corresponding catalogue quantities.
- scalingEquations defines the third line of Eq. (6), with d=3 and k=-2, \
differentiated with respect to the 21 shape fields.
- backgroundEquations eliminates eta and LAdS using the first two lines. The \
running varphi is included in fields and is set to zero in the tabulated \
reference slice. 
- BackgroundRules[x] gives field substitutions.
- BFStable[x] returns a Boolean; \[LineSeparator]- continuousSymmetryGroup[x] \
returns the continuous group name; \[LineSeparator]- discreteSymmetryGroup[x] \
returns the identified discrete symmetry modulo the connected continuous \
group H0.
- MassSpectrum[x, sector] returns numerical levels with multiplicities and \
their definitions.  The displayed values give M^2L^2 for bosonic fluctuations \
and M L for fermionic fluctuations.
- BackgroundSummary[x] returns the key properties as an association; \
\[LineSeparator]- BackgroundTableData[] returns these associations for all \
backgrounds.
- BackgroundResidual[x] returns the 21 shape-equation residuals. \
\[LineSeparator]- CheckBackground[x] also checks the first two lines of Eq. \
(6), returning the largest absolute residual and Below threshold only when it \
is strictly below 10^-10. \[LineSeparator]- CheckAllBackgrounds[] displays \
these checks for all backgrounds.

Discrete symmetries are verified subgroup results modulo H0, without a \
completeness claim or an implied direct product with H0. D8 denotes the \
dihedral group of order 8; None found means no additional component was found \
within the search performed, and does not assert its absence. \
\>", "Abstract",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9988025877246933`*^9, 3.998802665383087*^9}, {
   3.9988029533640327`*^9, 3.9988029636521797`*^9}, {3.998982297903219*^9, 
   3.9989823041095047`*^9}, {3.998982446944971*^9, 3.998982673747984*^9}, 
   3.9989828256090584`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"df26af14-08c8-47df-a845-\
cf5cfc971f16"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Initialisation (Run, do not edit. This can take up to ~30 seconds)\
\>", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9989643823385696`*^9, 3.9989643824021626`*^9}, {
  3.9989696379782734`*^9, 3.998969642836666*^9}, {3.998982273151596*^9, 
  3.9989822943701687`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7298ba20-eb47-b342-bf83-\
a99ab2a1dee9"],

